From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenAI coding assistant <assistant@local.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] kboot: honor an explicit T6050 simpledrm-only display trial

Local MIT-licensed adaptation of the existing T6050 DCP handoff. Keep all
DCP display nodes disabled on an explicit opt-out, before checking DCP
registers or inherited DARTs. Leave the chosen simple framebuffer and its
memory exclusion untouched. No marker preserves the existing DCP path.

The isolated J714s GPU-simpledrm DT uses this to test GPU rendering without
Linux DCP takeover. Native firmware scanout remains running; this is not a
DCP power-off request. The original loader and installed boot object are
not changed by this separate build profile.
---
diff --git a/src/kboot.c b/src/kboot.c
--- a/src/kboot.c
+++ b/src/kboot.c
@@ -2331,8 +2331,16 @@
     static const u32 disp_sids[] = {0, 16};
     int path[8];
     u64 vram_base = 0, vram_size = 0;
+    int dcp = t6050_dcp_node();
 
-    if (t6050_dcp_node() < 0)
+    if (dcp < 0)
         return 1;
 
+    if (fdt_getprop(dt, dcp, "apple,m1n1-simpledrm-only", NULL)) {
+        if (!t6050_dcp_find_nodes(&nodes))
+            bail("DCP handoff: malformed simpledrm-only display bindings\n");
+        printf("DCP handoff: simpledrm-only requested; skipping DCP hardware checks\n");
+        return t6050_dcp_set_status(&nodes, "disabled");
+    }
+
     if (!t6050_dcp_find_nodes(&nodes) || !t6050_dcp_running() ||
